virglrenderer: Venus refuses draws with a descriptor set or index buffer never bound

What: vkr keeps, per command buffer, which descriptor sets were bound at each bind point
since vkBeginCommandBuffer and whether an index buffer was (#624).
- Each graphics and compute pipeline gets the sets its shaders use: the bits the SPIR-V
  scan's walk (vkr_spirv_bindings_ok, from virgl-venus-spirv-scan.patch) finds in the
  functions an entry point reaches, collected in the layout callback vkr_stage_shader_ok
  already passes, before a scan of chained code is freed. A variable only listed in a
  SPIR-V 1.4 interface does not count, so vkr counts fewer sets than Vulkan's static use.
  Unknown (no check) for a pipeline without a layout, one that links libraries, and one
  that takes descriptor buffers. One mask per create info index, set on the pipeline
  objects that are made before the driver's call, so a partial failure or
  VK_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED keeps each pipeline's own.
- vkCmdBindPipeline copies the pipeline's mask (a later destroy does not matter);
  vkCmdBindDescriptorSets and vkCmdPushDescriptorSet mark their sets at their bind point,
  vkCmdBindDescriptorSets2 and vkCmdPushDescriptorSet2 by their stages (the compute stage
  marks the compute point, any graphics, task or mesh stage the graphics point, both when
  both are named); vkCmdBindIndexBuffer and vkCmdBindIndexBuffer2 mark the index buffer.
  Begin, reset and a pool reset clear it all; a secondary starts with none (it inherits no
  state); vkCmdExecuteCommands leaves the primary's as they were.
- Every draw and dispatch is refused when the bound pipeline uses a set to which nothing
  was bound at that point since the begin (VUID-vkCmdDraw-None-08600, the same VUID for
  each draw and dispatch). The four indexed draws (vkCmdDrawIndexed, -IndexedIndirect,
  -IndexedIndirectCount, vkCmdDrawMultiIndexedEXT) are refused without an index buffer
  bound since the begin unless the guest turned maintenance6 on (-None-07312). With
  maintenance6 that draw is legal: after every check passed, vkr binds the NULL index
  buffer (VK_INDEX_TYPE_UINT32) on the driver's handle once per recording, as the app
  could have.
Why: MoltenVK reads that state when it encodes the command buffer (at vkQueueSubmit in
QEMU, at vkEndCommandBuffer with prefill). On the M1 Max (Apple7), straight to the driver
with robust buffer access on (work/v624-unset, 3 runs per case in KosmicKrisp, MoltenVK and
MoltenVK prefill, each also under libgmalloc; 900 runs, 0 GPU restarts): a set the shader
uses that was never bound SIGSEGV in bindMetalResources (<- prepareDraw / prepareComputeDispatch,
a NULL set slot at 0x28) in 18 of 18 plain MoltenVK submits (graphics set 0, graphics set 1
with only set 0 bound, compute set 0), and with prefill at the end or the submit depending on
the heap; an indexed draw without an index buffer SIGSEGV in -[AGXG13XFamilyRenderContext
drawIndexedPrimitives:...] <- MVKCmdDrawIndexed::encode (a nil buffer, 0x20) at 6 of 6 plain
submits and 6 of 6 prefill ends; a NULL index buffer bound with maintenance6 works in all four
MoltenVK modes. KosmicKrisp crashed in none.
Left alone: a set bound with an incompatible layout, descriptors never written, push
constants never set (with and without maintenance4) and vertex buffers never bound: no crash
on either driver at the end or the submit, so they stay with the drivers; what the GPU then
reads stays robust buffer access's. After vkCmdExecuteCommands the primary keeps its masks
(Vulkan leaves its state undefined there, so an app binds again): a primary that draws with a
pipeline bound only inside a secondary is not checked for sets. The push descriptor template
calls have no handler (the guest driver sends them as plain pushes).
Upstream: OmacVM policy (ADR 0065).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the u- cases of case_unset; those that record a
refused draw or submit also under libgmalloc).

